Imho, the things that differenciate pudding-farming and poly-pile/... is  
that pudding farming can effectively leads to an unbounded amount or  
resources. Iirc, all others resources are only present in a finite bounded  
quantity in each games but pudding farming, via death drops, can generate  
any number of items.

That, imho, makes it different from other in game "abuse" (unwanted  
features/...).
Similarly, eXplore mode or savescumming leads to an unlimited resource  
(HPs), thus effectively removing most of the constraints of the game.

More or less, anybody is capable of ascending after reaching the  
castle/pudding farming/eXplore mode/... and the game becomes more or less  
a no brainer at this point. This is exactly the reason why you don't  
ascend : once you have all that you need, the game bores you.
I guess that if you pudding farm, you'll probably stop as soon as the farm  
starts going well because the game becomes "99% ascended" or so.

